docs {
  ## Kick

  Disconnect an online player.

  - Method and path: `POST /api/v1/players/{{playerName}}/kick`.
  - Path parameters: `{{playerName}}` — character name, case-insensitive, letters and digits only
    (max 24). A name that fails this pattern returns `404 not_found`.
  - Query parameters: none.
  - Body: none.
  - Signature headers: `X-GM-Timestamp`, `X-GM-Nonce`, `X-GM-Signature`, plus the write header
    `X-GM-Actor: {{gmActor}}`. All are set by `collection.bru`.
  - Write gate: `GmApi.AllowWrites = 1` (else `403 writes_disabled`).
  - Permission: `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_KICK` (510).
  - Target: online character. The API refuses the actor's own account (`409 cannot_target_self`)
    and any account with security at or above the actor's (`403 forbidden_target_security`).
  - Success: `200` with `{"status":"ok"}`. Audit rows: `pending` then `success`.
  - Failure: `403 forbidden`, `404 target_not_found` when offline, `409 cannot_target_self`,
    `500 audit_failed`, `503 world_unavailable`.

  Kick is the last request in a full collection run because it disconnects the target. Send it
  deliberately.
}
